{"id": "EUVD-2026-97582", "enisaUuid": "7baef863-d6cf-3378-abe6-1a34afdfd422", "description": "ImageMagick 7.1.0-20 before 7.1.2-32 contains a use after free vulnerability in the -fx option that occurs when a memory allocation fails during a specific operation. Attackers who can supply crafted -fx expressions under memory pressure can trigger freed memory access, causing crashes or memory corruption.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T16:04:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T18:06:44", "baseScore": 2.0, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:P/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-v2x3-wpmg-c4w6", "https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/fb743d60700c9bc350c3d2a0b48b998bdabc466c", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/imagemagick-7.1.0-20-before-7.1.2-32-use-after-free-via-fx-option"], "aliases": ["GHSA-ccrh-8v96-4jhw", "CVE-2026-109280"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.11, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "46444c25-757d-381a-9c27-f815c0d34396", "product": {"name": "ImageMagick", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}, "product_version": "7.1.0-20 <7.1.2-32"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "573c940f-9390-3344-8dcd-747d02c58cb1", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}], "isExploited": false}